[$in title:["Structs"]]
[$in description:["Nominal structs, construction, fields, deferred anonymous records and receiver methods in Moth."]]
[$in head:[language_theme_head]]

[navbar]
[sidebar]
init_docs_sidebar()!
[section, $md:
    # Structs

    A struct creates a nominal type with named fields. Two structs remain
    different types even when their fields match, unlike structural record
    systems.

    Receiver methods use ordinary top-level function declarations in the same
    file as the type. Their first parameter shows shared or mutable access.

    Runtime anonymous records are accepted deferred design. Their local hidden
    types keep nominal identity and use the shared MON construction notation.
]

